 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? I' start with kindling on ground, then add bigger branches until the fire is going. Avoid soaking the wood with water. They do, they soak up the water and the fire goes out slowly, which is useful if you' in a tent. A good rule is not much bigger than your cooking pot. Make sure there's no green left in it, tea won't oxidize properly if there's still grass in it. Make sure it' completely out before you go to bed, and never leave it unattended. Wild fires are one of the main reasons people get evicted.",
